{"name":"Clay","hex":"#b66a50","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Clay","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname originating as an occupation.","A male given name transferred from the surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Clay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clay","blocks":[{"text":"Clay is a type of fine-grained natural soil material containing clay minerals. Most pure clay minerals are white or light-coloured, but natural clays show a variety of colours from impurities, such as a reddish or brownish colour from small amounts of iron oxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Boulder_clay_cliff_south_of_Withernsea_%28geograph_6054962%29.jpg/330px-Boulder_clay_cliff_south_of_Withernsea_%28geograph_6054962%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clay","wikidata":"Q42302"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Clay_magnified.jpg/500px-Clay_magnified.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Clay_magnified.jpg/500px-Clay_magnified.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 23,500 times magnified electron micrograph of smectite clay","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClay_magnified.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Italian_and_African-American_Clay_Miners_in_Mine_Shaft.jpg/500px-Italian_and_African-American_Clay_Miners_in_Mine_Shaft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Italian_and_African-American_Clay_Miners_in_Mine_Shaft.jpg/1280px-Italian_and_African-American_Clay_Miners_in_Mine_Shaft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.